{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take Aaron</b> This passage was spoken seven days before the erection of the Tabernacle, for there is no earlier and later in the Torah — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 8:2). But why reverse the words of the living Elohim? Moreover, He commanded in the passage of \"On the first day of the first month\" (Exodus 40) regarding the entire erection of the Tabernacle and the vesting of Aaron and his sons and the anointing of all of them, and there Scripture relates Moses' action concerning the erection and mentions nothing about Aaron and his sons until this place. How could He separate one matter into two passages and delay what should have come first? Rather, the correct understanding is that it was said that he was commanded concerning the erection of the Tabernacle on the twenty-third of Adar and he erected it, and as soon as the Tabernacle stood in its place, immediately HaShem — who dwells upon the cherubim — called to him and commanded him concerning the sacrificial offerings, all these passages from the beginning of Vayikra until here, for He wished to teach him the procedure for all the offerings and their laws before he would offer any of them at all, for the consecration offerings include a sin-offering, a burnt-offering, and peace-offerings, and they would not know all their laws except from these passages that He preceded for him. And afterward He said to him, \"Take Aaron and his sons with him\" (Leviticus 8:2), to urge him at the time of action concerning what He had told him at the beginning (Exodus 29:1): \"And this is the thing that you shall do to them to consecrate them to minister to Me,\" and so on. And He added here (Leviticus 8:3): \"And all the congregation, assemble them at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting\" — that he should perform it in the presence of all of them, so that they would know that HaShem chose Aaron and his seed. And according to the straightforward way, Moses was commanded regarding the work of the Tabernacle before the incident of the calf, and when the Holy One, blessed be He, was appeased and promised him that His Shekhinah would dwell among them, he understood on his own that the commandment of the Tabernacle remained in its place, and he commanded Israel concerning it, as I explained in the passage of Vayakhel (Exodus 35:1). And after they completed the work, he was told the passage of \"On the first day of the first month, on the first day of the month, you shall erect the Tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting\" (Exodus 40:2), and there he was told \"And you shall bring near Aaron and his sons\" and so on (ibid. v. 12). And behold, he knew that Aaron and his sons too retained their dignity and their belovedness before the Place. And now He returned and urged him on the first day of consecration and at the time of action. And behold, all the passages are in their proper sequence, except that He preceded \"And the cloud covered the Tent of Meeting\" (ibid. v. 34), which is on the eighth day of consecration according to the opinion of our Sages (Sifra, beginning of Shemini), in order to arrange the entire matter of the erection of the Tabernacle, for so is the way of Scripture everywhere — to complete a matter that it began."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Ramban cites the Sages' view (referenced as בת\"כ, Sifra) that the cloud covering the Tent (Exodus 40:34) occurred on the eighth day of consecration; the parenthetical source reference follows the standard editions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:47.102244052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}